.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP 
A position in one top-level item: the owner of the bytes, the bytes and an offset\&. 

It holds no decoded value\&. Each member function reads the bytes at the offset when it is called\&. \fBcbor::lazy::view()\fP and \fBcbor::lazy::adopt()\fP set the data members\&. A copy of a lazy is a second position in the same bytes\&. Several threads read one lazy at the same time\&. A \fR\fBnodelist\fP\fP is the result of a path that selects many nodes\&. A lazy made with \fR\fBcbor::lazy\fP{}\fP holds no top-level item; each member function then throws \fRstd::logic_error\fP\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
cbor::lazy::adopt(bytes) → std::expected<lazy, error>
cbor::lazy const copy = *doc
.fi
.PP
 
.PP
.nf
message: [1, 2]
call: cbor::lazy const copy = *doc
result: lazy of [1, 2]
call: copy\&.at(1)\->get<int>()
result: 2

.fi
.PP

.PP
\fBExceptions\fP
.RS 4
\fIstd::logic_error\fP a member function of a lazy that holds no top-level item 
.PP
.nf
    // bytes: a std::string with [1, 2]
    auto const doc = cbor::lazy::adopt(std::move(bytes));
    cbor::lazy const copy = *doc;
    auto const second = copy\&.at(1)\->get<int>();  // 2
    // cbor::lazy{}\&.size() throws std::logic_error
.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
